lity, stress resilience, technical competence (weather, computers). Concerns: interpersonal (crew cooperation, professional communication), memory for numbers could affect attention/accuracy.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. Strengths: decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence. Concerns: communication, teamwork, adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Weaknesses: regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: temperament, possibly crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some concerns. Which candidate balances? Candidate B has strong reliability and stress handling, but interpersonal issues (nasty remarks) could be serious for crew cooperation. Candidate C has good decision making and calmness, but egocentric and communication issues. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving, but hot temper and know-it-all attitude. Candidate A has leadership and anticipation but show-off and not open to ideas.\n\nWhich is least concerning? Maybe Candidate B's nasty remarks could be severe. Candidate D's hot temper also severe. Candidate C's egocentric and communication difficulty also severe. Candidate A's show-off and not open to ideas also problematic but maybe less severe? Show-off could affect crew morale, not open to ideas affects adaptability. All have issues.\n\nWe might need to ask other panel members for more info on certain criteria. For example, we don't know about Candidate D's stress resilience. Also we don't know about Candidate A's stress handling. Could ask.\n\nBut we need to make a contribution now. Perhaps we can start by recommending Candidate B, citing strengths, but note concerns. Or we could ask a question to get more info before final recommendation. However the instruction says each turn must include a recommendation. So we must state a vote. We can state provisional recommendation, maybe Candidate B, and explain why.\n\nLet's do that. Provide evidence: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concern: nasty remarks, weak memory for numbers. But overall reliability and stress resilience are critical for long-distance flights. So we recommend B.\n\nProceed."}
